ive_lock_no_fcntl.py)"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Wrap each marker operation in `with sibling_exclusive_lock(marker_path, lock_name=MARKER_LOCK_NAME):` and catch `(OSError, NoExclusiveLegError)` at the with-boundary — the context manager's `locked` guard already satisfies AC #2, and NoExclusiveLegError propagates out for the fallback path, so no new selector code is needed in marker.py.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Consider reusing fsutil.sibling_exclusive_lock(marker_path, lock_name=MARKER_LOCK_NAME) instead of open-coding take_blocking_exclusive/release_exclusive, because it already provides the fd lifecycle and the 'release only if a lock was taken' guard that AC-2 requires and is the established pattern across 4 existing _store consumers.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'reuse rebar._store.lock_kernel.take_blocking_exclusive ... release_exclusive keeps the existing explicit-unlock-before-close shape ... marker.py must catch that befo